commit 5e7e5eb0f8657c37bef670555e9ff96624d096e6
Author: Hidde Beydals <hidde@hhh.computer>
Date:   Tue Nov 3 13:19:39 2026 +0100

    plumbing: storer, Look up an object's type from its header

    Telling a commit from a blob meant reading the object. For a packed
    delta that applies the delta to its base, so learning the type of a
    32 MiB blob stored as a delta built the whole blob. Git looks up the
    type alone, from the object headers (`odb_read_object_info`):
    upload-pack parses a have without checking its hash and discarding
    trees [1], and for a blob or tree that reads only the type [2].

    Add `storer.EncodedObjectTypeStorer`, an optional interface whose
    `EncodedObjectType` returns an object's type, and
    `storer.EncodedObjectType`, which uses it when the storer implements
    it and reads the object otherwise. Filesystem storage reads a loose
    object's header, and a packed object's through the new
    `Packfile.GetTypeByOffset`, which follows OFS_DELTA and REF_DELTA
    bases through their headers without inflating anything. A REF_DELTA
    whose base is in another packfile is read in full. Memory and
    transactional storage implement it too.

    The loose header read now closes the object file, which
    `EncodedObjectSize` left open: `objfile.Reader` closes only its zlib
    stream. Both lookups also close the `Packfile` they open for a packed
    object, which `EncodedObjectSize` did not, so each call left the pack
    pinned.

    [1]: https://github.com/git/git/blob/v2.54.0/upload-pack.c#L522-L549
    [2]: https://github.com/git/git/blob/v2.54.0/object.c#L345-L376

    Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
    Signed-off-by: Hidde Beydals <hidde@hhh.computer>

